<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Bernicia</h1><p class="st-meta">547 CE – 654 CE (approx.) · capital Bamburgh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The northern Anglian kingdom based on the fortress of Bamburgh, whose kings united with Deira to create Northumbria.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxon-chronicle">Anglo-Saxon Chronicle</a> dates Bernicia to 547, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ida-of-bernicia">Ida</a> took the kingship and built <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/earldom-of-bamburgh">Bamburgh</a>. Its people were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angles">Angles</a> who settled the coast between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-tees">Tees</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firth-of-forth">Forth</a> among the British population. The British name Bryneich suggests the kingdom took over an earlier British territory.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Bernicia's kings were warriors whose power rested on tribute and plunder. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelfrith-of-northumbria">Aethelfrith</a> defeated Aedan of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dal-riata">Dal Riata</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-degsastan">Degsastan</a> in 603 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britons-celtic-people">Britons</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chester">Chester</a>, then seized <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-deira">Deira</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswald-of-northumbria">Oswald</a> brought Aidan from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iona">Iona</a>, who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindisfarne">Lindisfarne</a> in 635, and royal sites such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yeavering">Yeavering</a> show grand halls.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu</a>, Bernicia and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-deira">Kingdom of Deira</a> were joined permanently after 654, forming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-northumbria">Kingdom of Northumbria</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/earldom-of-bamburgh">Bamburgh</a> remained a royal fortress and later the seat of the Earldom of Bamburgh.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-bernicia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Bernicia" width="320" height="333"><figcaption>Image: myself · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northumbria.rise.600.700.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>547 CE – 654 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bamburgh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ida, Aethelfrith, Oswald</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglo-Saxon paganism; Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bernicia, Bryneich</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=600&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bernicia" aria-label="Kingdom of Bernicia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4642 281 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Bernicia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4962 537L4976 582M4962 537L4945 553"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4976 582h0M4945 553h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4962 537h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4962 537h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bamburgh. <a href="/atlas?year=600&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bernicia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
